00:09:14,399 --> 00:09:20,399
Chadwick Aaron Boseman (; November 29, 1976 – August 28,
2020) was an American actor and playwright.

12
00:10:04,799 --> 00:10:10,799
Through his two-decade career, he appeared in a number of projects spanning both blockbuster and independent films, and received various accolades, including a
Golden Globe Award, a Screen Actors Guild Award, and a Primetime Emmy Award, in addition to nominations for an Academy Award and a BAFTA Award.

13
00:10:55,199 --> 00:11:01,199
Born in South Carolina, Boseman studied directing at Howard
University and began his career in theatre.

14
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:51,600
Boseman won a Drama League Directing Fellowship and an acting AUDELCO, along with
receiving a Jeff Award nomination for his 2005 play Deep Azure.

15
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:42,000
Transitioning to the screen, his first major role was as a series regular on the NBC drama Persons Unknown
(2010) and he landed his breakthrough role as baseball player Jackie Robinson in 42 (2013).

16
00:13:26,399 --> 00:13:32,399
He continued to portray historical figures, starring as singer James Brown in
Get on Up (2014) and as Thurgood Marshall in Marshall (2017).

17
00:14:16,799 --> 00:14:22,799
Boseman achieved international fame for playing the Marvel Comics superhero T'Challa
(Black Panther) in the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU) from 2016 to 2019.

18
00:15:07,199 --> 00:15:13,199
He appeared in four MCU films, including an eponymous 2018 film.

19
00:15:57,600 --> 00:16:03,600
As the first Black actor to headline an MCU film, he
was also named in the 2018 Time 100.

20
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:54,000
Boseman's final performance as the character in the
Disney+ anthology series What If...?

21
00:17:38,399 --> 00:17:44,399
(2021) earned him a posthumous Primetime Emmy Award for
Outstanding Character Voice-Over Performance.

22
00:18:28,799 --> 00:18:34,799
In 2016, Boseman was diagnosed with colon cancer.

23
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:25,200
He kept his condition private, continuing to act until
his death from the illness in 2020.

24
00:20:09,599 --> 00:20:15,599
For his final film role, the drama Ma Rainey's Black Bottom (2020), he received the Golden Globe and SAG
Awards for Best Actor, along with a posthumous nomination for the Oscar in the same category.
